  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "The Sperner reduction needs only a flat disc",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Two-kind knot spheres with local Kasteleyn signs. (1) The frames are flat at three-point faces and have label holonomy -1 at each of the six digons, so the flat states of FLAT-STATES-20261107-001A (one violated line, at the vortex) exist on every two-kind sphere wherever six disjoint cut paths reach the digons. (2) The reduction of one-sided Sperner_m of FLAT-STATES-20261107-001B uses only a corner-free lattice triangle of side 2m and such a flat state outside it, so it holds on every two-kind sphere with that triangle and cut paths from its boundary; with SPHERE-WIDTH-20261107-001B the knot then needs resolution width at least c m. (3) Hence width is at least c' r, for r the radius of the largest flat disc, and at most O(sqrt n) by planar separators: spheres with r of order sqrt(n) need width Theta(sqrt n), round or not. In the sample, grown lopsided spheres have r between 0.14 and 0.35 sqrt(n), against 0.25 sqrt(n) on the octahedral spheres, while a tube's r is bounded by its circumference.",
